steps.body:
As *Stacks, Queues, Deques, and Priority Queues* showed, a `std::priority_queue` built from two iterators takes a whole vector at once and arranges it into a heap in O(n), faster than pushing the items one at a time:

```cpp
std::vector<int> stones = {2, 7, 4, 1, 8, 1};
std::priority_queue<int> heap(stones.begin(), stones.end());
std::cout << heap.top() << ' ' << heap.size() << '\n';   // 8 6
```

To order by a computed key, give the heap a comparator type, like a struct with `operator()` from *Operator Overloading*. A heap's comparator answers "does `a` come out *after* `b`?", the reverse of a sort comparator. So `return da > db;` makes farther points come out later and puts the closest one on top:

```cpp harness
using Point = std::pair<int, int>;
{{code}}
std::vector<Point> pts = {{3, 3}, {1, -1}, {-2, 2}};
std::priority_queue<Point, std::vector<Point>, Farther> pq(pts.begin(), pts.end());
std::cout << pq.top().first << ' ' << pq.top().second << '\n';
```

```cpp
struct Farther {
    bool operator()(const Point& a, const Point& b) const {
        long long da = 1LL * a.first * a.first + 1LL * a.second * a.second;
        long long db = 1LL * b.first * b.first + 1LL * b.second * b.second;
        if (da != db) {
            return da > db;            // farther comes out later
        }
        return a.first > b.first;      // a tie: the smaller x comes out first
    }
};
```

The full type names the item, the container, and the comparator: `std::priority_queue<Point, std::vector<Point>, Farther>`. Squared distances skip the square root and stay exact, and `1LL *` computes them in `long long`.

example.code:
#include <iostream>
#include <queue>
#include <utility>
#include <vector>

using Point = std::pair<int, int>;

struct Farther {
    bool operator()(const Point& a, const Point& b) const {
        long long da = 1LL * a.first * a.first + 1LL * a.second * a.second;
        long long db = 1LL * b.first * b.first + 1LL * b.second * b.second;
        if (da != db) {
            return da > db;
        }
        if (a.first != b.first) {
            return a.first > b.first;
        }
        return a.second > b.second;
    }
};

int main() {
    int n = 0;
    int k = 0;
    std::cin >> n >> k;
    std::vector<Point> points(n);
    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
        std::cin >> points[i].first >> points[i].second;
    }

    std::priority_queue<Point, std::vector<Point>, Farther> pq(points.begin(), points.end());
    for (int i = 0; i < k && !pq.empty(); ++i) {
        Point p = pq.top();
        pq.pop();
        std::cout << p.first << ' ' << p.second << '\n';
    }
    return 0;
}

